WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.054 --> 00:00:07.666
As Swallow watched the flock go, he felt a little sad.

2
00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:10.504
He'd been born into that flock.

3
00:00:10.505 --> 00:00:14.280
The other birds were his family.

4
00:00:14.281 --> 00:00:16.295
He'd miss them.

5
00:00:16.296 --> 00:00:20.957
Still, he knew in his heart he'd made the right choice.

6
00:00:20.958 --> 00:00:26.957
"I never want to leave my love again," he thought.

7
00:00:26.958 --> 00:00:33.270
"This perfect rose will show her I care."

8
00:00:33.271 --> 00:00:36.011
Swallow flew back to the lake.

9
00:00:36.012 --> 00:00:39.832
He swooped and dove over the water.

10
00:00:39.833 --> 00:00:45.291
He flew in fancy circles and loops.

11
00:00:45.292 --> 00:00:49.500
"I hope my reed is watching," he thought.

12
00:00:49.501 --> 00:00:53.624
"She'll see what a great and fast flyer I am!

13
00:00:53.625 --> 00:00:57.478
And she'll love this rose."

14
00:00:57.479 --> 00:01:02.582
Swallow came in for a landing as the sun was setting.

15
00:01:02.583 --> 00:01:04.957
But something was wrong.

16
00:01:04.958 --> 00:01:08.749
His beautiful reed had disappeared!

17
00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:14.499
In her place was a bent and wilted brown reed.

18
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:19.332
"My most beautiful reed wilted!" Swallow thought.

19
00:01:19.333 --> 00:01:24.304
"This is the worst thing that has ever happened to me!"

20
00:01:24.305 --> 00:01:27.457
Swallow felt crushed.

21
00:01:27.458 --> 00:01:34.999
But then his situation got worse. A cold wind began to blow.

22
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:40.624
Swallow shivered. "Brr! Leader was right.

23
00:01:40.625 --> 00:01:46.832
I'll freeze here. I need to find my flock right away."

24
00:01:46.833 --> 00:01:52.522
Swallow dropped the rose where his love stood wilting and took off.

25
00:01:52.523 --> 00:01:55.082
He flew as fast as he could.

26
00:01:55.083 --> 00:01:58.999
But the wind was sharp and strong.

27
00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.499
And he didn't see the flock anywhere.

28
00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:05.525
"I'll find them in the morning," he thought.

29
00:02:05.526 --> 00:02:12.374
"For now, I just need a warm place to sleep."

30
00:02:12.375 --> 00:02:16.291
Swallow looked around the town.

31
00:02:16.292 --> 00:02:20.332
"There's that beautiful statue.

32
00:02:20.333 --> 00:02:25.541
It's the perfect place to spend the night."

33
00:02:25.542 --> 00:02:30.193
Swallow landed between the statue's two feet.

34
00:02:30.194 --> 00:02:33.637
"It's nice and warm here," he thought.

35
00:02:33.638 --> 00:02:38.437
Swallow tucked his head under his wing.

36
00:02:38.438 --> 00:02:42.361
Nearby two women were talking loudly.

37
00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:48.624
"My gown for the king's ball is going to be beautiful!" one said.

38
00:02:48.625 --> 00:02:53.166
"But that lazy seamstress still hasn't finished it!"

39
00:02:53.167 --> 00:02:56.832
"Why not?" asked the other.

40
00:02:56.833 --> 00:03:03.283
"Something about her son. I think he has a cold."

41
00:03:03.284 --> 00:03:09.291
Swallow, who loved beautiful things, wished he could see this lovely gown.

42
00:03:09.292 --> 00:03:12.999
"But I must leave early in the morning," he thought.

43
00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.582
He closed his eyes.

44
00:03:15.583 --> 00:03:22.374
Plop! A drop of rain fell on his head, then another, and another.

45
00:03:22.375 --> 00:03:30.541
"Oh bother!" he grumbled. "This isn't a good place to sleep after all."

46
00:03:30.542 --> 00:03:36.157
Swallow flew upward. He expected to get soaking wet.

47
00:03:36.158 --> 00:03:41.832
But there were no clouds. And there was no rain.

48
00:03:41.833 --> 00:03:44.722
Swallow blinked in surprise.

49
00:03:44.723 --> 00:03:52.743
The water was coming from the statue!

